          "text": "James purchased a certain baseball card on January 1. The function $f ( x )=75 ( 1.04 )$\n$x$ , where $0 \\le x \\le 10$ gives the predicted value, in dollars, of the baseball card $x$ years after\nJames purchased it. What is the best interpretation of the statement “ $f ( 6 )$ is approximately\nequal to 95” in this context?"
